<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<LightningComponentBundle xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>67.0</apiVersion>
    <isExposed>true</isExposed>
    <masterLabel>Deal Summary</masterLabel>
    <!--
        The description below is 227 characters (counted, not estimated). The Metadata API caps
        it at 255 and ONLY a
        deploy catches a breach - Jest, the SLDS linter and code review have all passed a
        258-character one in this repo. Count it before editing, and keep this comment INSIDE
        the root element (a comment above the root breaks sf at source conversion).
    -->
    <description>Latest NDA, LOI and PSA status for one sale, with the signed-NDA count. Ungated: it renders on every disposition stage. Each row fails soft, so a permission gap on one object degrades a single line instead of blanking the card.</description>
    <targets>
        <target>lightning__RecordPage</target>
    </targets>
    <targetConfigs>
        <targetConfig targets="lightning__RecordPage">
            <!--
                🔴 RESTRICTED TO Disposition__c (code review W5, 2026-08-20). Without this the card
                could be dropped on ANY record page, and it would not error there: every read behind
                it is WHERE Disposition__c = :id, which matches no rows rather than throwing, so a
                misplaced instance renders a confident, permanent EMPTY summary that looks exactly
                like a sale that has not started. The controller now also refuses a foreign Id at the
                server (code review C4) - this is the declarative half of the same guard, and it is
                the half that stops the mistake being made at all.

                The ELEMENT form. The objects= ATTRIBUTE form is rejected by the Metadata API - see
                marketDataSync.js-meta.xml, where that was measured.
            -->
            <objects>
                <object>Disposition__c</object>
            </objects>
            <!--
                🔴 THIS PROPERTY IS NOW THE ONLY DECLARATION OF recordId FOR THIS CARD - KEEP IT.
                Resolved 2026-08-20: Disposition_Record_Page no longer carries a
                componentInstanceProperties block for this component. The empty one it had was
                deleted, so the card now matches the three siblings on that page that are known to
                work, and recordId is supplied by the record page context against the declaration
                below. Delete this element and there is nothing left on either side that names
                recordId.

                An earlier version of this comment described the FlexiPage defect as OPEN and listed
                two candidate fixes pending another agent's decision. That decision has been made -
                the FlexiPage side was chosen - and this file was correct to leave the property
                alone. ⚠ Do not restate the claim that an empty-valued property block BREAKS the
                card: it was formally retracted as unproven, since dispositionMain carries the
                identical block and renders in production.
            -->
            <property name="recordId" type="String" />
        </targetConfig>
    </targetConfigs>
</LightningComponentBundle>
